12   onSelectSymbol: (name: string) => void;
13 }
14
15 export default function SearchOverlay({ visible, onClose, onSelectSymbol }: SearchOverlayProps) {
```

The component renders a `<Modal visible={visible} transparent animationType="fade" ...>` (line 47) and uses Fuse.js fuzzy search over `P5_SYMBOLS` (lines 21-38). Its `handleClose` (lines 40-44) clears the query, dismisses keyboard, and calls `onClose`.

## Summary

The requested feature is **already implemented** in `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/[id].tsx`:

- The Run button (lines 893-911) does NOT use React Native's `onLongPress` prop; instead it uses `onPressIn`/`onPressOut` with a custom 2000ms timer (`longPressTimerRef`, lines 567-582).
- Short press → calls `handleRun` (line 580) → posts `runSketch` to the WebView (lines 557-565).
- Long press (≥2s hold) → `setSearchVisible(true)` (line 572), which opens `<SearchOverlay>` (mounted at lines 972-978).
- `SearchOverlay` accepts `{ visible, onClose, onSelectSymbol }` (see `src/components/SearchOverlay.tsx` lines 9-13); `onSelectSymbol` navigates to `/ref?symbol=<name>`.

No edits are required for this feature to function; everything is wired end-to-end.
